<section id="A2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.3 </span>Baselines</h3>

<div id="A2.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">We compare our method against several generative baselines for OOD detection, including Improved CD </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib70" title="" class="ltx_ref">70</a>]</cite><span id="A2.SS3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, DoS </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib46" title="" class="ltx_ref">46</a>]</cite><span id="A2.SS3.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, TT </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib51" title="" class="ltx_ref">51</a>]</cite><span id="A2.SS3.p1.1.10" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, WAIC </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">5</a>]</cite><span id="A2.SS3.p1.1.13" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">,
NLL,
IC,
DDPM-OOD </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">3</a>]</cite><span id="A2.SS3.p1.1.16" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">,
LMD </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">36</a>]</cite><span id="A2.SS3.p1.1.19" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">,
DiffPath </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">35</a>]</cite><span id="A2.SS3.p1.1.22" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">. We use the official repositories for each method, along with diffusion models trained under the EDM framework </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">26</a>]</cite><span id="A2.SS3.p1.1.25" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> and the Glow model </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib45" title="" class="ltx_ref">45</a>]</cite><span id="A2.SS3.p1.1.28" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">. For the Glow-based baselines (DoS, TT, WAIC), we follow  </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib46" title="" class="ltx_ref">46</a>]</cite><span id="A2.SS3.p1.1.31" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">. In DoS, we extract three statistics—the log-likelihood, latent log-probability, and Jacobian log-determinant—and fit Kernel Density Estimators (KDE) on the training data for each, summing across statistics to obtain the final score. For TT and WAIC, we adopt the sample-wise versions from  </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib46" title="" class="ltx_ref">46</a>]</cite><span id="A2.SS3.p1.1.34" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">: TT measures the deviation of an individual sample’s likelihood from the training-set average, while WAIC is computed from five independently trained models using the mean and variance of their log-likelihoods. For diffusion-based baselines, we compute NLL using the official implementation from OpenAI’s improved diffusion Github repository</span><span id="footnote1" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">1</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">1</sup>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">1</span>
              
              
              
              
              
              
              
            <a href="https://github.com/openai/improved-diffusion" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://github.com/openai/improved-diffusion</a></span></span></span><span id="A2.SS3.p1.1.35" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> and derive IC by combining this NLL with PNG compression. Other methods (DDPM-OOD</span><span id="footnote2" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">2</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">2</sup>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">2</span>
              
              
              
              
              
              
              
            <a href="https://github.com/marksgraham/ddpm-ood" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://github.com/marksgraham/ddpm-ood</a></span></span></span><span id="A2.SS3.p1.1.36" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, LMD</span><span id="footnote3" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">3</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">3</sup>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">3</span>
              
              
              
              
              
              
              
            <a href="https://github.com/zhenzhel/lift_map_detect" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://github.com/zhenzhel/lift_map_detect</a></span></span></span><span id="A2.SS3.p1.1.37" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, DiffPath</span><span id="footnote4" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">4</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">4</sup>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">4</span>
              
              
              
              
              
              
              
            <a href="https://github.com/clear-nus/diffpath" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://github.com/clear-nus/diffpath</a></span></span></span><span id="A2.SS3.p1.1.38" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">) are implemented using their official repositories.</span></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.4 </span>Dataset and Models</h3>

<div id="A2.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">We follow the official train/test splits when training diffusion models.
For validation, we randomly sample 500 in-distribution (InD) and 500 OOD images; for testing, we sample a disjoint set of 500 InD and 500 OOD images.
All images are resized to </span><math id="A2.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="32\times 32" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">32</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">32</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">32\times 32</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.SS4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.
All diffusion models are trained using the EDM framework of </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">26</a>]</cite><span id="A2.SS4.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
